KNOWNBUG
packed_element_assignment1.sv
--bound 2
^\[main\.p0\] always \(##1 main\.a1 == 165\): PROVED up to bound 2$
^\[main\.p1\] always \(##1 main\.a2 == 165\): PROVED up to bound 2$
^\[main\.p2\] always \(##1 main\.a1\[1\] == 4'b1010\): PROVED up to bound 2$
^\[main\.p3\] always \(##1 main\.a2\[0\] == 4'b1010\): PROVED up to bound 2$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
The RTL construction places the elements of packed arrays as it does
for unpacked arrays, i.e., the element with the left index of the
declared range in the least significant position. In a packed array,
the element with the left index is the most significant (1800-2017
7.4.1), which is what the lowering of reads assumes. The elements are
hence written in reverse order.
